QNX: treat aarch64le as aarch64

On QNX, CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR is "aarch64le" (uname -p on a Raspberry Pi 5).
detect_onnxruntime_target_platform.cmake copies it into onnxruntime_target_platform,
and the checks in CMakeLists.txt compare against exactly "aarch64", so on QNX
KleidiAI is reported as "not supported on this platform" and switched off, and the
fp16 and bf16 compiler checks are skipped. MLAS still matches "^aarch64.*".
Map the QNX name to the standard one next to the existing x86_64 fix in 0001.

--- a/cmake/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/cmake/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -12,6 +12,9 @@
 if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "QNX" AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL "unknown")
   set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR "x86_64")
 endif()
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "QNX" AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL "aarch64le")
+  set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR "aarch64")
+endif()
 
 # Disable fast-math for Intel oneAPI compiler
 if("${CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID}" MATCHES "IntelLLVM")
